  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "For a < 1 and x < 1.1, Excel uses TOMS 654 double-precision st200 branch bounds with shared Kahan expm1, forcing even LSBs when P < 0.5",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, when 0 < a < 1.0 and 0 < x < 1.1 (unit scale x / beta), gratio computes z = S(a * ln(x)) with x87 PC64 operations and selects the upper-complement branch st200 using TOMS 654's double-precision (iop = 1) bounds: z >= -ln(2) (-0x1.62e42fefa39efp-1, 0xbfe62e42fefa39ef) when x <= 0.5, and S(a - x) < 0.25 when x > 0.5. Single-bit straddles at x = 0x3fd965fea53d6e3c vs 0x3fd965fea53d6e3d (a = 0.75) and x = 0.5 vs next_up(0.5) (a = 0.8125) establish both seams with zero bits of slack. Inside st200, Excel computes expm1(z) via its shared Kahan excel_expm1_internal(z) routine (not Morris's gratio_rexp rational) and forms P = 0.5 + (0.5 - qans), which by Sterbenz's lemma gives an even LSB (bit 0 = 0) on every output with P < 0.5 (85 of 85 across consecutive-x sweeps). Separately, for CHISQ.DIST(2*y, 2*a, TRUE) at a > 20 and y < 1.1, Excel exits the anomalous a > 20 lower-series branch at y == 1.1 (0x3ff199999999999a) while poisson_mass keeps compensated exp until y > 1.1.",
  "status": "inferred",
  "basis": "Measured in cb11 (1,391 live Excel 16.0.20527.20196 calls, frozen_cb11_predictions.jsonl 141 of 240 vs 105 of 240 on prior master) and nx9 (nx9_probe1: 582 of 1,478 combined matches vs 525 for gratio_rexp and 464 for prior master). Landing nx9 on full witness banks raised GAMMA.DIST by +656 (78,209 -> 78,865 of 83,312), GAMMADIST by +15 (3,019 -> 3,034 of 3,139), GAMMA.INV by +567 (4,336 -> 4,903 of 10,860), and GAMMAINV by +149 (4,106 -> 4,255 of 6,163) with zero per-function regressions.",
  "inferred": "The exact internal code structure of Excel's a < 1, x < 1.1 st190 primary branch (which still shows a non-monotonic period-16/32 sawtooth) and the a > 20, y < 1.1 CHISQ.DIST branch remain inferred in part and are open.",
